==Prefectural Historic Sites== As of 1 May 2023, ninety-five Sites have been designated as being of prefectural importance.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bunka.go.jp/seisaku/bunkazai/shokai/chiho_shitei/todofuken.html |script-title=ja:都道府県別指定等文化財件数（都道府県分）|trans-title=Number of Prefectural Cultural Properties by Prefecture |language=Japanese |publisher=[[Agency for Cultural Affairs]] |date=1 May 2023 |access-date=24 June 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.pref.nagasaki.jp/bunkadb/taikei_ken.html |script-title=ja:県指定文化財 |trans-title=Prefectural Cultural Properties |language=Japanese |publisher={{ill|Nagasaki Prefecture|en|Nagasaki Prefecture|qid=Q169376|lt=Nagasaki Prefecture|1=Nagasaki Prefecture}} |date=26 February 2021 |access-date=24 June 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.pref.nagasaki.jp/shared/uploads/2020/11/1605164993.pdf |script-title=ja:長崎県の文化財一覧 |trans-title=List of Cultural Properties of Nagasaki Prefecture |language=Japanese |publisher={{ill|Nagasaki Prefecture|en|Nagasaki Prefecture|qid=Q169376|lt=Nagasaki Prefecture|1=Nagasaki Prefecture}} |date=1 October 2020 |access-date=24 June 2024}}</ref>
